\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
\lang american
Statement
\series default
:
 For any real matrix 
\begin_inset Formula $X\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times d}$
\end_inset

 we can write
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
X=U\Gamma V',
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\lang american
where 
\begin_inset Formula $U$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $V$
\end_inset

 are semi-orthogonal and 
\begin_inset Formula $\Gamma$
\end_inset

 is a diagonal matrix with non-negative entries.
 The dimensions of all matrices depend on 
\begin_inset Formula $r=rank(X)$
\end_inset

 see proof.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
\lang american
Proof
\series default
:
 Consider the symmetric matrix 
\begin_inset Formula $B=X'X\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}$
\end_inset

 (which can be shown in one line:
 
\begin_inset Formula $(X'X)'=X'X$
\end_inset

) that by the spectral theorem 
\begin_inset Formula $B$
\end_inset

 has 
\begin_inset Formula $n$
\end_inset

 orthonormal eigenvectors 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{v}_{1},\dots,\mathbf{v}_{n}$
\end_inset

.
 Furthermore this implies that the eigenvalues are non-negative:
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{align*}
\lambda_{i} & =\lambda_{i}\mathbf{v}_{i}'\mathbf{v}_{i}\\
 & =\mathbf{v}_{i}'\lambda_{i}\mathbf{v}_{i}\\
 & =\mathbf{v}_{i}'(X'X)\mathbf{v}_{i}\\
 & =(X\mathbf{v}_{i})'(X\mathbf{v}_{i})\\
 & =||X\mathbf{v}_{i}||^{2}_{2}\geq0.
\end{align*}

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\lang american
Now define the singular values 
\begin_inset Formula $\sigma_{i}\equiv\sqrt{\lambda_{i}}$
\end_inset

 and define 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{u}_{i}\equiv X\mathbf{v}_{i}/\sigma_{i}$
\end_inset

.
 The latter can be shown to be orthonormal for the collection 
\begin_inset Formula $i=1,\dots,r$
\end_inset

 where 
\begin_inset Formula $r=rank(X)$
\end_inset

